# Bond coupons are paid weekly and show in Economy as loan expenses, like a loan's weekly cost.
# Sells a ₡10,000,000 1-year bond against fixed finances (3.15%: ₡6,057.69 a week), makes its
# first coupon due, lets eight days pass so a full week is on the books, and repays it in
# cleanup. Costs the city about ₡12,000 of interest.
name city bond: weekly coupons show in the Economy loan expenses
bond-finances 0 100,000,000
issue-bond 1 10000000
bond-backdate 7
run-days 8
expect-log coupon ₡6,057.
expect-loan-expenses 6,000
cleanup:
redeem-new-bonds
